.TH QDIFF 1 "2026 May 14" "Qore 2.3" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qdiff \- command-line diff tool powered by the Qore Diff module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qdiff
[\fIoptions\fP]
\fIfile1\fP
\fIfile2\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBqdiff\fR computes and renders differences between two files using the Qore
\fBDiff\fR module.
It supports several output modes (unified, normal, side\-by\-side, inline
character and word diffs) and a structured data mode for JSON, YAML and Qore
input.
.PP
A file argument of \fB\-\fP reads from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Output modes"
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unified
Unified diff format (default).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-normal
Normal (traditional) diff format.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-side\-by\-side
Side-by-side columnar format.
.TP
.B \-\-chars
Character-level inline diff.
.TP
.B \-\-words
Word-level inline diff.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-data
Structured data diff (JSON, YAML or Qore).
.SS "General"
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-context =\fIN\fP
Lines of context (default: 3, unified mode).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width =\fIN\fP
Output width (default: terminal width).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stats
Show insertion / deletion / unchanged counts.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Exit 0 if files are identical, 1 if they differ.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Files are identical.
.TP
.B 1
Files differ.
.TP
.B 2
Error (missing file, invalid options).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qpatch (1),
.BR qore (1)
